00:01:50.411 --> 00:01:52.037
That's easy, that's 24, duh.

00:01:52.037 --> 00:01:53.872
- All right, I'll take it.

00:01:53.872 --> 00:01:56.158
11 times zero is not 11.

00:01:56.158 --> 00:01:58.096
I guess I still have some things to learn.

00:01:58.096 --> 00:01:59.711
Shout out to Miss Hanson, third grade.

00:01:59.711 --> 00:02:00.768
She taught me well.

00:02:00.768 --> 00:02:01.708
- You have to know math.

00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:03.472
You should know your
multiplication tables.

00:02:03.472 --> 00:02:04.839
You should just know how to multiply,

00:02:04.839 --> 00:02:05.628
divide, add, and subtract.

00:02:05.628 --> 00:02:07.346
At least that stuff, you gotta know it.

00:02:07.346 --> 00:02:08.750
You gotta know it.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.048
Keith Habersberger endorses math.

